      ],
      "content": "The Google Drive MCP server failed because it requires an OAuth 2.0 Client credentials file at `~/.config/google-drive-mcp/gcp-oauth.keys.json` to initiate authentication.\n\nBelow are the most effective CLI tools to interact with and fetch content from Google Drive:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: `rclone` (Recommended — Most Powerful & Mature)\n\n`rclone` is the industry standard CLI for cloud storage management (supports syncing, listing, mounting, and downloading).\n\n#### 1. Install via Homebrew\n```bash\nbrew install rclone\n```\n\n#### 2. Interactive Setup\n```bash\nrclone config\n```\n1. Type `n` for a new remote (e.g. name it `gdrive`).\n2. Choose `drive` (Google Drive).\n3. Leave Client ID/Secret blank to use defaults (or provide your own).\n4. Select scope `1` (Full access) or `2` (Read-only).\n5. It will automatically open your default browser to authenticate your Google account.\n\n#### 3. Listing & Fetching Content\n```bash\n# List all top-level directories / folders\nrclone lsd gdrive:\n\n# List directories recursively\nrclone lsd -R gdrive:\n\n# View a visual directory tree\nrclone tree gdrive: --dirs-only\n\n# List files inside a specific folder\nrclone ls \"gdrive:My Folder\"\n\n# Download a folder to local disk\nrclone copy \"gdrive:My Folder\" ./local-destination\n```\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: `gdrive` CLI (Lightweight & Drive-Specific)\n\nA dedicated, lightweight Go CLI specifically for Google Drive.\n\n#### 1. Install\n```bash\nbrew install gdrive\n```\n\n#### 2. Authenticate\n```bash\ngdrive account add\n```\n\n#### 3. Fetch Folders & Files\n```bash\n# List all folders\ngdrive files list --query \"mimeType = 'application/vnd.google-apps.folder' and trashed = false\"\n\n# Download a file or folder by ID\ngdrive files download <FILE_ID_OR_FOLDER_ID>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Using the Google Drive MCP Server\n\nIf you prefer to continue using the Google Drive MCP server directly within this IDE:\n\n1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console Credentials](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials).\n2. Create an **OAuth 2.0 Client ID** with Application type: **Desktop app**.\n3. Download the JSON credentials and save it to:\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p ~/.config/google-drive-mcp\n   mv /path/to/downloaded-credentials.json ~/.config/google-drive-mcp/gcp-oauth.keys.json\n   ```\n4. Once placed, running the MCP tool will prompt you to complete the one-time browser login, creating `~/.config/google-drive-mcp/tokens.json`."
